1 & 1 \\
2 & 8 \\
3 & 27 \\
4 & 64 \\
5 & 125 \\
6 & 216 \\
7 & 343 \\
8 & 512 \\
9 & 729 \\
\end{array}
\] We see that we only counted the $1$ twice. After listing all $21$ of these, we see that the only integer that was 555 itself, not less than $555,$ was $343 + 216 = 559$. Therefore， the sum is $21 - 1 = 20$ (we counted $1$ twice -- $1^2 = 1 = 1^3$) plus the $9 - 3 = 6$ perfect squares besides $1$. The final answer is $20 + 6 = \boxed{26}$.  [asy]unitsize(3mm);
